{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1478773-a-doubt-with-endowment-creation-in-2e","id":1478773,"title":"A Doubt with Endowment creation in 2E.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-13T10:26:27-07:00","id":1478773,"title":"A Doubt with Endowment creation in 2E.","content":"This is probably a dumb question because possibly I missed something while reading that section of the book, but I'd rather ask it and make sure I'm doing it right.<br /> If an Endowment is a weapon and is opposed by Defense like any other conventional attack, does that count as an opposed or contested roll when calculating the cost of the Relic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-13T17:11:32-07:00","id":1478806,"title":"","content":"It's not spelled out in the text. But so far as I can tell, the answer is yes.<br /> <br /> For example, if you look at Tools of the Trade, a 1L attack costs +2 (since according to the table, a weapon modifier is equal to value - 1), the immobilized tilt costs +1, and the willpower point cost gives back -1, leaving +2 points unaccounted for. Presumably, there's a hidden -2 from the fact that actually using the 1L attack requires a resisted action i.e. a normal Brawl attack, which brings the net cost to 0.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-14T01:01:25-07:00","id":1478825,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much for helping me with the question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25189-dagurasu","name":"Dagurasu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}